#
# SGLang v0.5.18 + our SM121 build patches. Created 2026-08-28 to track the
# v0.5.18 line (released 2026-08-22, 710 PRs / 212 contributors). NOT BUILT and
# NOT GPU-VALIDATED yet: rebuild, acceptance gate and a real serving run before
# it goes in front of anything. Read OPEN RISK A first, it currently blocks the
# gate.
#
# THE HEADLINE: nothing moved the way v0.5.17 moved (the sgl-kernel tree stays
# at python/sglang/kernels/aot/, so SGL_KERNEL_DIR is unchanged), but three
# things changed underneath us:
#   1. Upstream's torch pin jumps 2.11.0 to 2.13.0 (triton 3.7.1, torchvision
#      0.28.0, torchcodec 0.15.0; torchaudio stays 2.11.0). We keep building on
#      the 2.12/cu132 base, which for the first time puts us BELOW the upstream
#      pin instead of above it. The Dockerfile pins torch/vision/audio/codec out
#      of the resolution (PIP_CONSTRAINT + missing_deps --ignore), so the build
#      itself is unaffected, but see OPEN RISK D.
#   2. nvidia-cutlass-dsl moves 4.6.0 to 4.6.2 upstream, and the release notes
#      credit it with fixing an FA4 startup regression on Blackwell. We follow:
#      CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION 4.6.1 to 4.6.2.
#   3. Every compiled-kernel cache moves under SGLANG_CACHE_DIR (#32434). See
#      the DEPLOY NOTE block at the bottom of this header.
# flashinfer stays at 0.6.17: it is still the newest STABLE release (0.6.18 only
# exists as rc10 as of 2026-08-28) and v0.5.18 has moved its own pin up to
# exactly 0.6.17, so for the first time in this recipe line our flashinfer pin
# and upstream's agree.
#
# ── DELTA vs sglang-0.5.17-sm121.recipe ─────────────────────────────────────
#   1. SGLANG_VERSION 0.5.17 to 0.5.18, SGLANG_REF to v0.5.18.
#   2. SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT "-v0.5.17" to "-v0.5.18". NOT cosmetic: upstream
#      reshaped the Blackwell gencode block in aot/CMakeLists.txt. The explicit
#      "-gencode=...sm_103a" is gone, replaced by sm_100f on CUDA 12.9+ ("covers
#      all sm_100, sm_103, sm_107, sm_10x") with sm_100a as the pre-12.9
#      fallback. Hunk 2 of sgl-kernel-arch-prune-v0.5.17.patch targets the old
#      shape and FAILS on this ref, which would abort the build in the container
#      dry-run. The pruned RESULT is unchanged (sm_121a on aarch64 plus the
#      arch-neutral --compress-mode=size, nothing else).
#   3. CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION 4.6.1 to 4.6.2 (upstream's new pin, see the block
#      below). Requires a fresh rmsnorm smoke test on the built image.
#   4. FLASHINFER_VERSION: UNCHANGED at 0.6.17. Now identical to upstream's own
#      pyproject pin, so OPEN RISK E of the v0.5.17 recipe is closed.
#   5. SGL_KERNEL_DIR: UNCHANGED (python/sglang/kernels/aot). The tree did not
#      move again; the kernel package is still "sglang-kernel", now version
#      0.4.6.post1 (was 0.4.5), same CMakeLists / Makefile / csrc layout.
#   6. TRANSFORMERS / KERNELS / HF_HUB / AUDIO / ACCELERATE / BASE_IMAGE:
#      UNCHANGED. v0.5.18 still pins transformers==5.12.1 and kernels>=0.14.1,
#      <0.15. PyPI-latest for the record, all deliberately NOT taken:
#      transformers 5.16.1, kernels 0.16.1 (violates the upstream constraint),
#      nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.6.3 / 4.7.1 (past the upstream pin and, for 4.7,
#      past the API window flashinfer #3922 migrated to), huggingface_hub 1.29.0
#      (our 1.26.0 is a FLOOR and is already satisfied by it).
#   7. TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT stays "-v0.5.16" and the marlin patch stays ON;
#      both re-verified against v0.5.18, see PATCH VERIFY. tilelang itself is
#      still pinned to 0.1.11 upstream (PyPI is at 0.1.13), so the 0.1.8-era
#      uint8-view compat hunk is still the right shape.
#   8. Upstream dependency churn that rides along with the ref (informational,
#      none of it a knob here): sgl-kernel 0.4.5 to 0.4.6.post1, sgl-deep-gemm
#      0.1.5.post1 to 0.1.5.post3, quack-kernels >=0.6.1 to ==0.6.4, NEW
#      sgl-deep-ep==0.1.0 (DeepEP now ships as a released wheel instead of being
#      built from source) and NEW cuda-tile==1.6.0rc5, torchao and helion are
#      REMOVED. apache-tvm-ffi stays pinned at 0.1.11 in the pyproject, i.e.
#      unchanged from v0.5.17. See OPEN RISK E for cuda-tile.
#
# ── PATCH VERIFY (2026-08-28, non-GPU, against raw v0.5.18 source) ───────────
#   OK sgl-kernel-arch-prune-v0.5.18.patch        REGENERATED (2 hunks)
#   OK sgl-kernel-disable-fa3-v0.5.18.patch       regenerated, content identical
#   OK sgl-kernel-skip-sm90-target-v0.5.18.patch  regenerated, content identical
#   OK sgl-kernel-skip-flashmla-v0.5.18.patch     regenerated, content identical
#      Produced the same way as the -v0.5.17 set: apply in build order, fix the
#      one drifted hunk by hand, re-diff each step, so all four land with ZERO
#      fuzz and ZERO offset and the four "dgxarley ..." marker pairs (8 total)
#      are present afterwards. Re-applying the whole set to pristine v0.5.18
#      reproduces the expected tree byte for byte. The -v0.5.17 files correctly
#      FAIL here (arch-prune hunk 2), so a recipe that forgets to move the
#      suffix aborts loudly instead of building unpatched.
#      Only two things changed in that CMakeLists between the refs: the bundled
#      triton source URL (3.6.0 to 3.7.1) and the Blackwell gencode block.
#   OK sglang-dsv4-mtp-marlin-v0.5.14.patch       applies (hunk 1599, offset 153)
#   OK sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch  clean (path
#      python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/tilelang_kernel.py unchanged)
#   OK Dockerfile chain re-verified against current scitrera origin/main
#      (unchanged since 44a9e8b, 2026-06-09): sm121, kernels-pin, audio-deps,
#      cutlass-dsl-pin, accelerate, dsv4-flashmla, dsv4-mtp-marlin-tilelang,
#      hf-hub-floor plus build-image-sh-podman, all apply (offsets only).
#   NO sgl-kernel-sm121.patch                     target still gone, GATED OFF
#      (unchanged since v0.5.16, PR #30448).
#
# ── OPEN RISKS, validate before this recipe is promoted ──────────────────────
#   A. RUNTIME patches (roles/k8s_dgx/files/sglang_patches/) WILL DRIFT, and at
#      least three targets are already known to have moved in v0.5.18. This
#      currently BLOCKS the acceptance gate (it exits 1 on any ANCHOR-DRIFT and
#      runs before the push), so expect to re-target before a build promotes:
#        * p34: sglang/srt/model_executor/model_runner_kv_cache_mixin.py is
#          GONE. The model runner was split into
#          srt/model_executor/model_runner_components/ (kv_pool_runtime.py,
#          attention_backend_setup.py, cuda_graph_setup.py, layer_setup.py, ...).
#          p34 is the LIVE-PROVEN GLM-5.2 DSA path, so this one is load bearing.
#        * p35 and p30: srt/layers/attention/dsa/triton_paged_mqa_logits.py and
#          .../torch_paged_mqa_logits.py are GONE from srt/. The kernel side now
#          lives under python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/
#          (paged_mqa_logits.py, cutedsl_paged_mqa_logits.py). p30 also WRITES a
#          torch backend module into the old directory, so both the read and the
#          write side need re-pathing.
#      Everything else p11/p30/p34/p37/p50/p51 touches still exists at its
#      v0.5.17 path (weight_utils.py, dsa_backend.py, dsa/dsa_indexer.py,
#      dsa/paged_mqa_logits_backend.py, forward_mla.py, trtllm_mha_backend.py,
#      hybrid_attn_backend.py, qwen3_5.py, modelopt_quant.py), but "the file is
#      there" is not "the anchor is there": run the gate, do not assume.
#      Reminder from the v0.5.17 cycle: p50/p51 are self-gated OFF on >= v0.5.17
#      (fix is upstream) and stay in the ConfigMap only for instances still
#      pinned to older images.
#   B. INHERITED from v0.5.16, still open: moe_runner_backend cutlass / triton
#      for NVFP4 is gone (#30448), so nvidia/Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-NVFP4 (cutlass)
#      and Minimax-M2.5 @ PP=4 (triton) still need re-testing or re-pinning, and
#      compressed-tensors NVFP4 MoE with apply_router_weight_on_input=True still
#      asserts instead of running. See TURBOQUANT.md.
#   C. NEW in v0.5.18, from the release's own "Breaking Changes":
#      * The DSV4 fused MHC post+pre path is ON BY DEFAULT, explicitly including
#        SM12x (#35214, #34019). In v0.5.17 that was an opt-in we had never
#        exercised. Any DeepSeek-V4 profile is on a new default path here.
#      * MoE deferred finalize is ON BY DEFAULT on the NVFP4 + flashinfer_trtllm
#        path with an unfused non-TP1 shared expert, i.e. the DeepSeek-V3 family
#        (#33618). Escape hatch: SGLANG_ENABLE_MOE_DEFERRED_FINALIZE=False.
#      * Unified-cache out-of-window SWA slot freeing is ON BY DEFAULT (#34653).
#        Escape hatch: SGLANG_OPT_UNIFIED_CACHE_FREE_OUT_OF_WINDOW_SLOTS=False.
#      * torchao integration REMOVED (#34304), remote media downloads bounded to
#        64 MiB with redirect validation (#34892), 22 benchmarks deleted.
#      Carried over from v0.5.17 and still true: the SM120 FP8 per-tensor GEMM
#      backend is cuBLAS (#31961), and AOT bmm_fp8 / router GEMM / fused A GEMM
#      are gone from the kernel wheel in favour of flashinfer.
#   D. TORCH GAP INVERTED. Upstream now wants torch 2.13.0 (triton 3.7.1); our
#      base image is 2.12.0/cu132, so SGLang code written against a 2.13 API
#      would fail at import or first use rather than being harmlessly newer than
#      the pin. Nothing in the build enforces the pin (constraints file plus
#      missing_deps --ignore torch/torchaudio/torchvision/torchcodec), and the
#      unpinned `uv pip install triton` step resolves against whatever is
#      current. There is no 2.13 base to move to today: scitrera's newest
#      published tag is still 2.12.0-v1-cu132 (2026-06-09), so a bump would mean
#      a new scripts/build_pytorch_base_image.sh recipe. Smoke-test imports on
#      the built image before trusting it.
#   E. NEW dependency shapes that the missing_deps step will try to install:
#      * cuda-tile==1.6.0rc5 has NO wheel on PyPI for that version, only a
#        wheel-stub sdist that redirects the build backend to pypi.nvidia.com
#        (where cp312 manylinux2014_aarch64 does exist). If the build fails
#        there, the fix is an --extra-index-url https://pypi.nvidia.com (or
#        pre-installing cuda-tile) rather than unpinning it.
#      * sgl-deep-ep==0.1.0 ships a cp312 aarch64 wheel, verified present.
#      Note missing_deps.py only checks PRESENCE, not version, so anything the
#      base or an earlier step already installed will not be moved to the new
#      pin. That is what keeps apache-tvm-ffi at the resolved 0.1.13-post level
#      the flashinfer ABI wants instead of the pyproject's 0.1.11.
#   F. INHERITED: NVFP4 ATTENTION on SM121 (flashinfer #3897) is still only
#      KERNEL-level verified (2026-07-28 on spark5), never validated end to end
#      through SGLang with a real uniform-NVFP4 model. Judge output quality by
#      pattern-grep plus token distribution plus tail, not by finish_reason.
#      Same for the flashinfer 0.6.17 FP4 numerics fix (#3932): it landed after
#      the last quality matrix, so re-run those checks, do not carry verdicts.
#   G. SM12x work in v0.5.18 we have NOT exercised, several of which overlap
#      with what p30 to p35 do by hand (check for redundancy BEFORE re-porting
#      anchors, same lesson as the v0.5.16 fp8_paged_mqa_logits_torch_sm120
#      absorption): the DSV4 fused MHC default above, the paged_mqa_logits move
#      into kernels/ops, and the overlapped checkpoint staging option
#      (--startup-weight-load-mode overlap, #32017) which is independent of arch
#      and may be worth measuring on the slow JuiceFS-backed model store.
#
# ── DEPLOY NOTE: SGLANG_CACHE_DIR (#32434) ──────────────────────────────────
# Triton, FlashInfer, Inductor, DeepGEMM and the CUDA driver cache all move
# under SGLANG_CACHE_DIR, so the FIRST launch on this image recompiles once.
# Setting any of TRITON_CACHE_DIR / FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE /
# SGLANG_DG_CACHE_DIR / TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR / CUDA_CACHE_PATH keeps that one
# where it is. We already set FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE explicitly in
# roles/k8s_dgx/tasks/sglang_instance.yml, so the expensive flashinfer JIT cache
# is NOT affected; the DeepGEMM cache is, and is the other expensive one.
#
# Prerequisite: xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.12.0-v1-cu132 present on the
# build host (scripts/build_pytorch_base_image.sh, see ensure_base_image_present
# in build_sm121_image.sh).
#
DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
TARGET=runtime

BASE_IMAGE=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.12.0-v1-cu132

# flashinfer 0.6.17 (2026-08-11), UNCHANGED from the last state of the v0.5.17
# recipe and still the newest STABLE release: 0.6.18 exists only as release
# candidates (rc10 as of 2026-08-28) and the stable-only pin policy holds. As of
# v0.5.18 this is ALSO upstream's own pin (flashinfer_python[cu13]==0.6.17 in
# python/pyproject.toml), so we are no longer running ahead of SGLang here.
#
# The SM12x rationale from the v0.5.17 recipe carries over unchanged: #3932 (b12x
# FP4 quantization numerics fix plus a separate input_global_scale, the reason
# W4A4 output quality has to be re-measured rather than carried over), #4253
# (mm_fp4 SM120 dense GEMM synced to b12x HEAD), #4130 (cute SM120 fused MoE
# SwiGLU), #4117 (GDN WY decode on SM121), #3903 (trtllm_allreduce on SM12x),
# #4161 (xqa flaky test on spark), #4380 (DSV4 sparse-MLA top-k consolidation,
# scoped to _DECODE_DSV4_DISPATCH so the p34/p35 GLM-5.2 path is untouched),
# #4101 (CuTe-DSL runtime FLOOR back to 4.5.2, a floor and not a ceiling).
# Older, still valid: #3897 NVFP4 attention on SM121, #3838 SM120 qk_correction
# and lse correctness, #3960 GDN CuteDSL as sm_121a, #3922 cutlass-dsl 4.6 API
# migration.
#
# Wheels re-verified 2026-08-28 on https://flashinfer.ai/whl, all three packages
# exist at 0.6.17 including the one that matters for arm64:
#   flashinfer-python    0.6.17  (py3-none-any)
#   flashinfer-cubin     0.6.17  (py3-none-any)   <- not on PyPI, only here
#   flashinfer-jit-cache 0.6.17+cu130 manylinux_2_28_aarch64
#
# Roll-back order: 0.6.16.post3 (what the first 0.5.17-sm121 build shipped and
# passed the acceptance gate on), then 0.6.16 (GPU-cleared on 0.5.16-sm121),
# then 0.6.15.post1 (live-validated on 0.5.15.post1-sm121).
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.15.post1
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.16
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.16.post3
FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.17

# transformers 5.12.1 - exactly v0.5.18's pyproject pin (==5.12.1, unchanged
# since v0.5.15). Do NOT bump past the SGLang ref (no perf benefit, transformers
# is not in the inference hot path; PyPI-latest 5.16.1 is irrelevant here).
TRANSFORMERS_VERSION=5.12.1

# kernels 0.14.1 - exactly v0.5.18's constraint (kernels>=0.14.1,<0.15,
# unchanged). PyPI-latest 0.16.1 violates it. PERF-NEUTRAL on SM121: the only
# hub-loaded kernel (sgl-flash-attn3) is hard-disabled on GB10 and has no
# sm_121/ARM64 builds.
KERNELS_VERSION=0.14.1

# nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.6.2 - BUMPED from 4.6.1 to match v0.5.18's pyproject pin
# (nvidia-cutlass-dsl[cu13]==4.6.2, was 4.6.0 on v0.5.17). The release notes
# credit the CuTeDSL bump with fixing an FA4 startup regression on Blackwell.
# Force-reinstalled late in the build; the explicit pin stays mandatory because
# NVIDIA has shipped different wheel CONTENT under the same version number
# before (the 4.5.2 mlir_global_dtors 'data' ICE, see
# reference_cutlass_dsl_wheel_swap).
# NOT taken: 4.6.3 / 4.7.0 / 4.7.1 (PyPI-latest). flashinfer #3922 migrated off
# the APIs removed in cutlass-dsl 4.6 while keeping 4.5.x compatibility, which
# makes 4.6.x the explicitly-supported window; 4.7 is past it with nothing to
# gain, and 4.6.3 is newer than what upstream tests against.
# MUST GPU-verify on the built image before deploy (rmsnorm smoke test):
#   python -c "import flashinfer, torch; \
#     from flashinfer.norm import rmsnorm; \
#     x=torch.randn(4,512,device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16); \
#     w=torch.randn(512,device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16); \
#     print(rmsnorm(x,w).shape)"
# and confirm the DSL path is actually TAKEN (norm/__init__.py falls back to
# CUDA JIT SILENTLY when the DSL cannot target the arch, which makes the smoke
# test go green without ever compiling a DSL kernel):
#   _cute_dsl_supports_arch(12,1) / is_cute_dsl_arch_supported(12,1) -> True
#   norm._use_cuda_norm(cuda:0) -> False   (False means DSL, not CUDA JIT)
#   the *_cute symbols (rmsnorm_cute, fused_add_rmsnorm_cute, ...) all import
# Fallback: 4.6.1 (what 0.5.17-sm121 shipped), then 4.6.0, then 4.5.1.
# CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.6.0
# CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.6.1
CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.6.2

# Audio multimodal deps - see the 0.5.15.post1 recipe. SGLang pulls numba itself
# (numba==0.65.1); librosa is still needed (soundfile/audioread).
AUDIO_DEPS="librosa"

# accelerate - baked into the image (ModelOptModelLoader imports it).
ACCELERATE_DEPS="accelerate"

# huggingface_hub FLOOR (not an exact pin). Guards against the xet gated-repo
# download bug: hub PR #4394 (tree-listing cache) forwarded the REDACTED xetHash
# placeholder that the /tree API returns for GATED repos straight to hf_xet ->
# "Task error: Unable to parse string as hex hash value" on every fresh
# snapshot_download of a gated model (hf_preload job, shard jobs, model-download
# initContainer). hf_xet was never at fault. Fixed by hub PR #4595, released in
# v1.26.0 (2026-07-30). See FIXED_UPSTREAM_HF_XET_BUG.md. Neither hub nor hf_xet
# is pinned anywhere else in the build, so without this floor an unlucky
# re-resolve could quietly reintroduce the crash the moment the cluster stops
# setting HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET=1. Installed as the LAST pip action of the builder
# stage (dockerfile-hf-hub-floor.patch) so nothing can downgrade it afterwards.
HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION=1.26.0

SGLANG_VERSION=0.5.18
SGLANG_REF="v0.5.18"

# main-ahead sgl-kernel patch variant. Kept at 1 for provenance (the -v0.5.18
# files carry the mainahead content, the mscclpp link refactor is still in the
# tree), but SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT takes precedence in apply_patches(), so
# the -mainahead siblings themselves are not used on this ref.
SGL_KERNEL_MAINAHEAD=1

# Suffix of the four CMakeLists source patches to install under the canonical
# names. "-v0.5.18" = the -v0.5.17 edits regenerated against v0.5.18, where
# arch-prune hunk 2 additionally had to be REWRITTEN because upstream replaced
# the sm_103a gencode with an sm_100f/sm_100a branch. All four regenerated with
# zero fuzz and zero offset. Empty/absent in pre-0.5.17 recipes.
SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.18"

# Where the sgl-kernel tree lives inside the sglang checkout (moved there by RFC
# #29630 in v0.5.17), passed to the Dockerfile as ARG SGL_KERNEL_DIR (default
# "sgl-kernel", so older recipes are byte-identical). UNCHANGED in v0.5.18; MUST
# match the path in the patch variant above.
SGL_KERNEL_DIR=python/sglang/kernels/aot

# ── CORE SM121 JIT-header patch: TARGET STILL GONE (PR #30448) -> OFF ────────
# python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/moe/nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh has not returned in
# v0.5.18 (verified 2026-08-28) and cutlass_moe_fp4() is still absent; NVFP4 MoE
# runs through FlashInfer-CUTLASS on SM100/SM120/SM121, the backend our model
# profiles pin anyway (moe_runner_backend: flashinfer_cutlass). At 1 the
# in-container dry-run would abort the build. Consequence: see OPEN RISK B.
APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 FlashMLA kernel: DROPPED (native since v0.5.13) ──────────────
FLASH_MLA_REPO=
FLASH_MLA_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_REPO=
DSV4_KERNEL_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_ARCH=

# ── DeepSeek-V4 NVFP4 MoE: NATIVE since v0.5.14 (PR #25820) -> OFF ──────────
APPLY_DSV4_NVFP4_PR25820=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 EAGLE-MTP marlin branch + TileLang indexer compat -> ON ──────
# Unchanged rationale vs 0.5.17: HybridFp8NvFp4Config.get_quant_method still has
# no marlin branch for the MTP/nextn draft-MoE layers, and the TileLang uint8
# arg check still bites (tilelang is still pinned to 0.1.11 upstream). Both
# source patches dry-run-verified against v0.5.18 on 2026-08-28 (marlin: hunk at
# 1599, offset 153; tilelang: clean).
APPLY_DSV4_MTP_MARLIN_TILELANG=1

# Variant of the tilelang compat patch. "-v0.5.16" selects
# sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch: the path introduced by RFC
# #29630 (python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/) and only the uint8-view hunk,
# because upstream adopted the 2D alloc_shared half. That file name is a
# GENERATION label, not a ref restriction; the path and the hunk are unchanged
# in v0.5.18, verified clean. apply_patches() installs the selected variant under
# the canonical name, so the Dockerfile step is unchanged.
TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.16"

# ── Qwen3.6 ModelOpt mixed NVFP4: MERGED (PR #27906) -> OFF ─────────────────
# The OPEN dispatch fix #28099 is a RUNTIME patch in sglang_launch.sh and is
# unaffected by this flag (p21/p22); re-check Qwen3.6 live.
APPLY_QWEN36_MIXED_NVFP4_PR27906=0

IMAGE_TAG=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-sglang:0.5.18-sm121
